  "title": "Election Commission Withdraws SIR Declaration from Form 6 in India, with Congress Criticizing",
  "summary": "The Election Commission (EC) withdrew the SIR-related declaration from Form 6 in states where the electoral roll revision exercise concluded, citing the ECINET portal updates. The EC’s decision follows a meeting that determined the requirement would only apply during the exercise, marking a shift in the rules. Congress accused the EC of breaching constitutional standards and demanded immediate action to address concerns.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Election Commission (EC) withdrew the SIR-related declaration from Form 6 in states where the electoral roll revision exercise concluded.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EC’s decision follows a September 26 meeting of the full Commission, which decided the requirement would only apply during the exercise.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Congress accused the EC of breaching constitutional standards and demanded immediate action to address concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
